<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marvdasht</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marvdasht is a city and plain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a>. The fertile plain, watered by the Kur and Pulvar rivers, contains the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a>, Naqsh-e <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostam">Rustam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istakhr">Istakhr</a>, centres of Achaemenid and Sasanian power. In the tenth century the Buyid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adud-al-dawla">Adud al-Dawla</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/band-e-amir-dam">Band-e Amir</a> dam on the Kur to irrigate it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marvdasht.jpg" alt="Marvdasht" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: درفش کاویانی · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tachar_Persepolis_Iran.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
